HELIOS ADVANCE BBS SCRIPTING API EXCEPTION

Version 1.0

This is an additional permission under section 7 of the GNU Affero General
Public License, version 3 ("AGPLv3"), as published by the Free Software
Foundation. It supplements, and does not replace, the AGPLv3 under which the
Helios Advance BBS Program is licensed (see the LICENSE file for the full text
of the AGPLv3). In the event of any conflict, the AGPLv3 governs except to the
extent this exception grants additional permission.


1. Additional Definitions.

"The Program" (equivalently, "the HADV Engine") means Helios Advance BBS and all
of its source code and object code that is covered by the AGPLv3. This includes,
without limitation, the Go engine, its embedded Lua runtime, the implementation
of the public `bbs.*` scripting bindings, and any C, Go, or other code compiled
or otherwise linked into the Engine binary.

"Public Scripting API" means the public `bbs.*` Lua API namespace exposed by the
Engine for the purpose of implementing BBS menus, display, and user-flow logic.

"Eligible Script" means a Lua script, a theme, or a collection of Lua scripts
and theme assets that interacts with the Engine, if at all, solely through the
Public Scripting API, and that does not otherwise incorporate, embed, or link
any part of the Engine's source or object code, and does not modify or replace
the implementation of the Public Scripting API or any other part of the Engine.


2. Grant of Additional Permission.

You have permission to author, use, propagate, license, distribute, sell, or
keep private any Eligible Script under terms of your own choosing, including
terms that are incompatible with the AGPLv3.

Loading or running an Eligible Script together with the Engine, and conveying an
Eligible Script that is designed to be interpreted by the Engine, do not by
themselves cause the Eligible Script to be a "modified version" of, a "work
based on", or a covered work derived from the Program within the meaning of the
AGPLv3. Accordingly, such an Eligible Script is not subject to the requirements
of the AGPLv3, including the corresponding-source obligations of its section 13
(Remote Network Interaction), solely by reason of being loaded, run, or conveyed
for use with the Engine.


3. Preservation of Copyleft for the Engine.

This exception applies only to Eligible Scripts as defined above. It grants no
additional permission with respect to the Engine itself or to any work that is
not an Eligible Script.

In particular, a fork or modified version of the Engine, a modified or
alternative implementation of the Public Scripting API or its `bbs.*` bindings,
and any C, Go, or other code compiled or linked into the Engine binary remain
fully governed by the AGPLv3, including its section 13 network-interaction
requirements. Nothing in this exception permits the removal of, or non-compliance
with, the AGPLv3 as applied to the Engine.


4. Section 7 Status.

This Scripting API Exception is an additional permission within the meaning of
section 7 of the AGPLv3. As provided in that section, any recipient may remove
this additional permission from any covered work they receive; doing so leaves
the AGPLv3 alone in force for that copy of the Engine.
